WEBVTT

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:02.470
Banagher!

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:06.050
You're my hope.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:08.510
I entrust them all
to you, Banagher.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.180
Mr. Gilboa...

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.880
A news flash has arrived
from our Dakar press center.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.260
Here they come!

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:15.510
Fusion reactor shutdown confirmed.
No chain reaction.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.380
Intense heat source detected...
Incoming!

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:47.510
You're taking too long to launch!
What's the holdup?!

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:48.930
I need a sit-rep!

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:56.090
I still can't believe they're
attacking the capital.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.380
I've been waiting
for this moment!

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:29.720
Father, Mother...
It's all the Federation's fault!

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.050
Loni, enemy reinforcements
are coming.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:34.970
We've done enough!
The diversion worked.

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:37.760
Now we wait to hear from
the Garencieres Team.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:39.760
Roger.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:51.010
So, it has begun...
We must resolve this swiftly.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:56.090
Indeed... However, the key to
Laplace's Box, the Unicorn,

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:59.510
vanished in the battle that destroyed
the old prime minister's residence.

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:02.180
And remains missing.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:08.010
Nevertheless, if Master Cardeas
saw fit to choose him...

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:14.130
God is toying with us...

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:19.720
Or rather, has Cardeas'
"mankind's" dream been fulfilled?

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:29.430
Banagher, my flesh and blood...

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.630
(FROM THE SCORCHING EARTH)

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:39.970
Zeon remnants have remained dormant in
the three years since Char's Rebellion.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:43.800
Does this sudden act of terrorism
signal a new uprising by them?

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.880
Some pundits believe this to be
the opening salvo of a third- -

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:52.510
Damn it all... Why is he summoning me
out to his home at a time like this?

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.180
I protest the implication.

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:01.930
Unlike the attack on Lhasa
three years ago,

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:06.720
this one on Dakar cost the lives of
many government workers, as well.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:11.430
I must say, this mutual mudslinging
is most unproductive.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:16.550
I would prefer to have a more
constructive discussion, Ms. Martha.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:19.130
I'll cut to the chase, then.

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:22.720
Please hand over the VIP
that is currently in your care.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:26.550
What are you talking about?

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:29.720
It is in the best interests of both our
sides, as well as yours personally,

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.630
Chairman Ronan Marcenas.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:36.090
Leaving aside my interests for the
moment, what do you stand to gain?

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:40.470
I'll leave that to your imagination.
Deliver her to- -

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:45.470
Please contact me again
in two hours' time.

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:48.050
There is an urgent matter
that demands my attention.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:49.550
As you wish.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.550
I'm dying to ask the Chairman,

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:57.800
what "urgent matter" could be more
important than the Zabi orphan?

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:14.470
I know what a difficult situation
this puts you in. But she- -

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:15.760
You've fallen for her,
haven't you?

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:20.130
That's why you deserted
and fled here.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:25.050
It's just like when you ran away from
home, saying you wanted to be a pilot.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:29.090
I didn't expect you to get yourself
mixed up with the Box...

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:33.260
You need to learn the truth
behind the Marcenas family.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:38.880
Given the situation, that is the
only way that you will survive this.

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:46.590
Grant us your salvation.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:49.090
Salvation...

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:55.220
At present, the military
and the fire department

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:58.590
are doing everything they can
to locate survivors.

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:02.550
What should I do?
Banagher...

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.090
What nerve!

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:09.800
Riddhe?

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.050
Forgive me.

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:19.720
What is the matter?

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:22.880
I've learned that I come
from a shameful family.

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:24.470
Shameful?

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:30.050
My family, the Marcenas family, acts as
a mirror image of the Vist Foundation.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:33.510
That is how we have managed to survive
through the Universal Century.

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:38.970
I know my family will stop at nothing
to prevent the release of Laplace's Box.

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:41.510
Even using you as
a hostage again.

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:44.590
The only way to prevent that
is to get the Box

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:47.090
before either the Foundation
or the Neo Zeon.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:49.090
Either that, or destroy- -

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.180
Its key? The Unicorn?

00:08:56.840 --> 00:09:01.430
I've brought you to the
worst possible place.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:04.470
And here I thought
I could help you...

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:07.840
Come what may,
I'll protect you.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:11.050
So please, stay here.
By my side...

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:14.720
Don't leave me alone.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:24.630
Will... Will you become
a member of my family?

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:29.970
Leave Zeon and the Zabi family
and join the Marcenas family.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:32.220
If you did that,
even father would have to...

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:33.840
Even if it's just for show.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:38.260
You could put an end to this pointless
fighting and win your freedom.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:43.220
That kind of freedom... Would you
really call that being free?

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:48.220
Everything is clear.

00:09:58.090 --> 00:09:59.720
Ple Twelve.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:01.970
That's your name, isn't it?
Answer me.

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:07.590
You're to obey
your master's orders.

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:10.970
You aren't my master.

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:15.180
If you want to make me obey, you'll have
to try reconditioning or torturing me.

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:17.260
M-Mind your tone!

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:20.840
We've learned that reconditioning you
would be difficult.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:23.550
You were made too well.

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:25.720
Still, that is for the best.

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:31.680
I have no interest in a doll whose
memories can simply be swapped out.

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:33.430
What I truly want is...

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:43.470
The Mass Production Type Qubeley.
The machine you all used to pilot.

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:46.050
Artificially-created Newtypes.

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:48.760
Puppets that do the bidding
of their master.

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:55.260
Your soul is still held prisoner
within that machine.

00:10:55.300 --> 00:11:00.760
You were created as a tool of war by men
who knew nothing but spilling blood.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.800
Considering that true life is
born from a woman's womb,

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:05.970
don't you find that unnatural?

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:08.590
I am going to free you
from that machine.

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:27.180
This is a camouflaged Sleeves freighter
that made Earthfall some ten days ago.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:31.260
I've heard about the ruins
of Laplace being destroyed.

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:33.180
Are you saying that these
people were responsible?

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:37.260
I want you to use your ship
to locate them.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:41.590
In short, you wish to use the
Ra Cailum for personal reasons?

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:46.340
This ship was also involved in
the incidents at Industrial 7 and Palau.

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:48.930
As commander of the Londo Bell,
aren't you also concerned

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:51.970
about the safety of
the Nahel Argama?

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:55.340
At present, she is being
detained in Earth orbit.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:59.380
The order came from the
Vist Foundation via General Staff HQ.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:03.470
I don't want to be seen
as taking hostages,

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:05.680
so I've laid my cards
on the table first.

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:09.430
The Foundation is after
this ship, as well.

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:12.590
If we take it into custody first,
it will give us the upper hand.

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:14.720
What is so special
about this ship?

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:19.840
This ship is carrying something
called Laplace's Box.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:24.720
In the event you are unable to
capture it, I want you to destroy it.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.930
You give me
too much credit, sir.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:31.680
I've simply had a career slightly
outside the norm, I'm not- -

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:36.430
Captain a series of motherships for
Gundam types since the One Year War,

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:39.880
and you will naturally be seen as
a commander of a Newtype corps.

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:43.430
That does seem to be
my luck, sir.

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:49.050
An example of being taken advantage of
if you display your talents too overtly.

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:51.630
There is one other favor
I want to ask of you.

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:55.510
I have an unworthy son
who serves as a military pilot.

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:58.010
I would like you
to take him aboard your- -

00:12:58.050 --> 00:12:59.880
- What is it?
- Begging your pardon, sir.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:05.380
What is it, Doillon? I told you
I wasn't to be disturbed until...

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:11.800
The Lady Mineva has disappeared
from her room.

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:14.630
We are searching the vicinity
as we speak.

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:40.630
Sorry, I'm the last person you
want advice from on this,

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:44.430
but the only way to get the
mobile suits out is to crack the hull.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:49.130
We'll save that as a last resort.
That would wreck the Garencieres.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:54.970
Sir, if we don't link up with friendly
forces soon, the enemy will find us.

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:58.050
Even if they do say
their diversion worked.

00:13:58.090 --> 00:14:01.180
I still can't believe they
hit Dakar, of all places.

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:02.720
I can understand
how they feel.

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:08.720
After all, the people waiting on Earth
missed out on two Neo Zeon wars.

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:15.430
There's no telling what stunt they'll
pull next if we don't make contact.

00:14:15.470 --> 00:14:19.130
There's an oasis
about 60km east of here.

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:20.970
Let's make a quick trip there
by mobile suit,

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:23.260
then make contact with our allies.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:25.260
At this point,
wrecking the ship is- -

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:29.510
Rushing is pointless, and this won't
work if the Unicorn isn't operational.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:33.970
We could always tie up the kid inside
the cockpit and bring the whole suit.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:37.180
The next set of coordinates
the La+ program gave

00:14:37.220 --> 00:14:39.970
are in one seriously
inconvenient place.

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:42.720
Give me the map.

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:46.510
Damn it, what is he thinking?

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:49.510
Why the hell would he
bring you, of all people?

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:52.090
Bastard!

00:14:52.130 --> 00:14:56.680
Don't think we won't kill you just
because you're the Unicorn's pilot!

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:58.720
I'm not thinking that at- -

00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:07.430
I know that this is all my fault.
I killed Mr. Gilboa.

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:08.680
You bet your ass it is!

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:11.130
He could've put us down
safe and sound,

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:15.800
even with your Unicorn latched onto the
ship during atmospheric entry like that.

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:33.340
On the house.
Drink up.

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:36.380
I like the way you dig in.

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:39.340
It's nice to see a young lady who
isn't obsessed with good manners.

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:43.380
Thank you, I will.

00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:46.680
I haven't seen you around before.
Whereabouts do you hail from?

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:55.260
A Spacenoid, huh? Certainly explains
why I haven't seen you before.

00:15:58.550 --> 00:16:03.050
You sightseeing? There isn't much
around here to see.

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:05.720
Not at all. As someone born
and raised in space,

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:09.090
I'm happy to be able to
set foot on the ground.

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:13.630
To people like me, there are times
when gravity isn't kind.

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:18.340
Makes me wonder if my back wouldn't
bother me anymore if I went into space.

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:21.260
You have lived on Earth
your entire life?

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:24.300
Yeah. I'm too old
to leave her now.

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:34.180
My generation was raised on stories
of the bad old days

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:36.800
from our grandfathers
and grandmothers.

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:39.380
Sounds like things got pretty
terrible back then.

00:16:43.550 --> 00:16:45.590
They wanted to do
something about it,

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:49.680
so they founded the Federation and
got the space settlement thing started.

00:16:56.630 --> 00:17:01.840
Some folks say it was only the poor
that were forcibly discarded into space,

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:05.340
but there were a lot of people
who left of their own accord.

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:10.590
They were prepared to stay away
until the Earth's environment recovered.

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:15.630
But then the One Year War undid most
of the progress that had been made.

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:18.510
We're hopeless, aren't we?

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:25.630
Well, what can you do?
It all began out of good intentions.

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:27.800
Good intentions?

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:29.970
Both the Federation
and the space settlement

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:33.130
began with the hope of saving humanity.

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:38.380
Like wanting your business to succeed,
or making a better life for your family.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:42.550
But that can turn into something
better described as egotism.

00:17:42.590 --> 00:17:44.720
Maybe so.

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:49.130
But if we denied that,
this would be a sad world.

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:53.550
I guess there are some who can work for
the greater good at their own expense,

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:55.880
but there's something
shady about it.

00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:58.680
Like that Char guy
with the Neo Zeon.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:01.010
He said he was fighting for
the good of everyone,

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:03.180
even while he was dropping
asteroids on us.

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:08.470
Truth is, maybe he was just a guy
who never learned to love humanity.

00:18:08.510 --> 00:18:10.010
What can we do, then?

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:14.340
Hell if I know.
We never figured that out.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:19.220
I think we tried, but in the end,
we just postponed paying our debts,

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:23.130
and I spent my life regretting not being
able to do anything for you people.

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:27.260
It's all I can do to just
make you a cup of coffee.

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:42.010
I see...
I suppose you're right.

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:45.970
What can I possibly do?

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:52.340
The coffee was delicious.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:56.430
This alone made my coming
to Earth worthwhile.

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:04.050
Miss Audrey Burne.
Chairman Ronan is waiting.

00:19:04.090 --> 00:19:05.800
Come with us, please.

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:06.930
You're...

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:12.840
I am Mineva Zabi. I have no intention
of running or hiding.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:14.430
Stand aside.

00:19:35.130 --> 00:19:38.130
I'm having Mineva Zabi
brought here.

00:19:38.180 --> 00:19:41.590
I plan to use her as bait
to recapture the Unicorn.

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:43.550
She will probably obey, too.

00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:44.680
Yes, ma'am.

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:47.260
You can be the one
to give her the orders.

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:49.130
U-Understood.

00:20:14.090 --> 00:20:15.880
Why me?

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:18.800
Because you look like you have
the most time on your hands.

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:21.680
It's impossible. You can't walk
four days through a desert.

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:23.760
There's a way to do it.

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:36.430
Idiot.

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:40.470
Didn't I tell you to take regular sips
even if you're not thirsty?

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:42.510
Please, just leave me here.

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:45.970
Do you want me to tell you to
hang in there or something?

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:49.800
Please, leave me alone.
I'm sick of it.

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:52.550
Of being caught up in things
I don't understand, and being used.

00:20:52.590 --> 00:20:56.800
Sorry, I can't do that.
You're a pilot.

00:20:57.090 --> 00:21:00.220
Get out of the victim mindset
and quit sulking.

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:02.800
Gilboa would roll over
in his grave.

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:04.760
I didn't mean to kill him!

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:07.840
Mr. Daguza died, and my head
went completely blank.

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:11.260
If you can't forgive me,
just get it over with!

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:12.840
That's not true.

00:21:13.720 --> 00:21:16.880
Your eyes say that you don't
believe that for one minute.

00:21:16.930 --> 00:21:21.050
Those are the eyes of a man who decides
for himself how he lives and dies.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:23.880
So until you do die, put on
a brave face for others to see.

00:21:23.930 --> 00:21:27.090
A man's life is a struggle
until the day he dies.

00:21:31.550 --> 00:21:34.510
...try with all your might,
the path will show itself to you!

00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:37.130
You go fulfill your own role.

00:21:37.180 --> 00:21:41.260
I did... That's what I did!
For all I was worth!

00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:43.970
And look at what happened!

00:21:44.010 --> 00:21:49.970
I fought and killed in a mobile suit,
and now I'm walking across a desert!

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:53.220
What more am I supposed to do?!

00:21:53.260 --> 00:21:55.800
What do you want me to fight?!

00:23:38.130 --> 00:23:41.300
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam Unicorn

00:23:41.340 --> 00:23:43.260
BATTLE AT TORRINGTON

00:23:44.930 --> 00:23:48.300
awaken the Newtype that lies within you.
